  "task": {
    "source_message_id": 146,
    "speaker": "client",
    "text": "Here is the FAQ section. Please load it after adjusting anything that needs refinement.\n\nWhat is Harbor Quill?\nAs the live proof of concept for CORA (Community Outreach Response Automation), Harbor Quill demonstrates the first system through which independent creators can sell unlimited-mint NFT ebooks while rewarding readers with real commissions and prizes for promoting it.\nThe launch features my raw memoir novella, “Against the Current: Finding the Finish Line,” on Base. It is also my public effort to support my household's recovery after a six-figure property fraud.\nIf CORA succeeds, Harbor Quill will develop into ArchiveLedger, a community-owned public-good platform available to every creator.\n\nHow do buyers earn money?\n1. Earn a $10 instant commission whenever a buyer mints with your referral code\n2. Receive Small & Big Block prize tickets whenever somebody mints using your code\n3. ***If CORA proves successful, with zero guarantee of success or value***\nBuyers, affiliates, and tippers of “Against the Current: Finding the Finish Line” will receive a future ArchiveLedger governance-token allocation.\n\nHow do referrals work?\nEach NFT uses its token serial as its permanent referral code.\nBoth approaches work:\n→ Share the entire link\n→ Tell the buyer to “use referral 423”\nWhen your code is used, you immediately receive $10 and the current Small & Big Block prize tickets.\n→ If the mint has no referral code, the commission and tickets go to a random existing NFT holder.\n\nWhere do I find my referral code?\nYour code is the token serial, shown:\n- On the NFT itself\n- Inside its NFT metadata\n- On your Dashboard after minting\n- Optionally, in the confirmation email\n\nWhat are Small Block and Big Block prizes?\nSmall Block awards 8 × $900 approximately every ~2,400 sales from mints and secondary transactions.\nBig Block awards 9 × $6,000 approximately every ~180,000 sales from those same sources.\nEvery sale funds the pools forever.\n\nHow are winners selected?\nChainlink VRF performs the selection fully on-chain, with provable fairness and Basescan verification.\n\nWhat are Small & Big Block prize tickets?\nThese are entries for the active Small & Big Block drawings. Successful referrals provide 4 Small + 3 Big tickets, and additional tickets improve the chance of winning.\nAfter a block is drawn, its tickets expire and new referrals apply to the next blocks.\n\nHow do I claim my rewards?\n- $10 commissions → automatically transferred to your wallet\n- Prize wins → posted on the Winners page and claimable with one click at <http://harborquill.example>\n\nWhat are badges?\nOn-chain badges are attached to the NFT when referrals reach 5, 25, 125, 500+.\nThey currently provide cosmetic status and leaderboard flex. In the future, they may unlock token-gated chats, discounts, and other benefits.\n\nCan I mint with fiat (credit card)?\nYes. Transak supports cards, Apple Pay, and Google Pay.\n\nDo I need a wallet to participate?\nA wallet is not needed to mint with fiat. It is required, however, if you want to receive commissions, hold prize tickets, or sell or trade the NFT later.\n\nWhat blockchain is this on?\nThe project uses Base (Ethereum Layer 2), offering fast, inexpensive, and secure transactions.\n\nAre there any hidden fees?\nNo. Each mint costs exactly $30, and secondary sales have a visible $48 flat royalty.\n\nWhat happens if I sell my NFT?\nThe purchaser receives the book, the token serial as their referral code, all earned badges, and every active prize ticket; expired tickets remain expired.\n\nHow do I share my referral link/code?\nUse the Dashboard to copy the complete link or the token serial, then tell people to “use referral 423”.\n\nIs this a scam or pyramid scheme?\nNo. It is single-level only, and the complete source is verified on Basescan. I receive $8 from every mint and secondary sale forever, minus fiat fees; everything else supports commissions and prize pools.\n\nHow do I contact support?\nDiscord is not available yet and will launch only after real traction develops.\nFor now, DM @HarborQuill on X or email elias@harborquill.example.\n\nAnyone with further questions can DM @HarborQuill on X or contact elias@harborquill.example—I’m happy to assist."
  },
